{"t": 224.97, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE", "rationale": "Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) is used to boost the output voltage, which is critical for the weak excitation case (S4) where the piezo's open-circuit voltage is only ~1.9 V. By using a transfer inductor and synchronous switches, SECE can deliver a voltage to the output capacitor higher than the piezo's peak voltage. A Zener clamp (DZ33) is added to prevent overvoltage in strong excitation (S3), and a large output capacitor is used to minimize ripple (Vpp) and stabilize the output (dV).", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE", "rationale": "Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) is used to boost the output voltage, which is critical for the weak excitation case (S4) where the piezo's open-circuit voltage is only ~1.9 V. By using a transfer inductor and synchronous switches, SECE can deliver a voltage to the output capacitor higher than the piezo's peak voltage. A Zener clamp (DZ33) is added to prevent overvoltage in strong excitation (S3), and a large output capacitor is used to minimize ripple (Vpp) and stabilize the output (dV).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 5e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "G2", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 5e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "neg"}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzn", "n1"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n1", "n2"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 1e-05}, {"id": "Dz", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
